Linear Search:
Linear Search checks each element one by one until the required element is found.

Case	      Time Complexity
Best Case	       O(1)
Average Case	    O(n)
Worst Case    	  O(n)
Space Complexity	O(1)

Works on both sorted and unsorted arrays.
Best case occurs when the target is the first element.
Worst case occurs when the target is the last element or not present.
Simple to implement but slower for large datasets.
